Let $P(3,4,-1)$ and $Q(-1,2,3)$ be the end points of the diameter of a sphere.
$\therefore$ Length of diameter $=P Q\begin{aligned}
&=\sqrt{(-1-3)^{2}+(2-4)^{2}+(3+1)^{2}} \\
&=\sqrt{16+4+16}=\sqrt{36}=6 \text { units } \\
\therefore \quad \text { Radius } &=\frac{6}{2}=3 \text { units }
\end{aligned}$

Let the required point be $P(x, y)$. Then,

\begin{aligned}
4|y| &=\left(\sqrt{\left.(x-0)^{2}+(y-0)^{2}\right)^{2}}\right.\\
\Rightarrow \quad 4|y| &=x^{2}+y^{2} \\
\Rightarrow x^{2}+y^{2}-4|y| &=0
\end{aligned}
